# Normalize to LF in the repo. Render checks out on Linux, and mixed endings
# across Windows contributors would otherwise churn the diff on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated output: never touched by git's newline conversion.
#
# Filenames under site/assets carry a sha1 of their contents, and render.yaml
# serves them with `immutable` caching on the strength of that. If git rewrote
# line endings on checkout, the bytes served would no longer match the hash in
# the name they are served under. Marking the tree binary keeps the two in
# lockstep on every platform.
site/assets/** -text

# The original bundle is a build input, byte-identical to what was exported.
Client/** -text
